cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "NKG7 Structural Analysis"
message: "If you use this analysis, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Corvino
    given-names: Dillon
    email: dcorvino@uni-bonn.de
    affiliation: "University of Bonn"
abstract: >-
  In-silico structural and evolutionary characterisation of NKG7, testing the
  hypothesis that it functions as an ion channel. A tiered, gated computational
  campaign (structural-homology triage; three-predictor homo-oligomer prediction
  with reference-HOLE pore analysis) finds NKG7 is a claudin/Ca_V-gamma tetraspan
  that self-associates but forms no conducting pore, consistent with a
  scaffold / auxiliary-modulator role.
keywords:
  - NKG7
  - structural bioinformatics
  - ion channel
  - AlphaFold3
  - Boltz-2
  - Chai-1
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-07-14
